docs/requirements/decisions/proof-admissibility-hardening-execution-plan.md:1577:- A later closeout idle/max timeout preserves any already-observed validation disposition, evidence basis, and refusal reasons; only the later terminal result/layer changes to `timed_out` and `idle|max`. The command-level `done_prepare` budget is the exact sum of routine validation plus each enabled closeout phase once (five non-validation phases, plus DONE-required only when enabled). CLI named deadline errors propagate through routine verifier execution so a command deadline that lands between watchdog polling ticks retains `timeoutLayer=max`.
docs/requirements/decisions/proof-admissibility-hardening-execution-plan.md-1578-
docs/requirements/decisions/proof-admissibility-hardening-execution-plan.md:1579:- Closeout segments check the parent watchdog before and after each segment and await cooperative abort cleanup. Synchronous JavaScript is inherently non-preemptible, so it stops at the first deadline/checkpoint boundary. Pure in-process closeout segments spawn no descendants, making process-tree ESRCH evidence not applicable there; descendant cleanup is required and tested only for validation/phase paths that actually spawn children.
docs/requirements/decisions/proof-admissibility-hardening-execution-plan.md-1580-
docs/requirements/decisions/proof-admissibility-hardening-execution-plan.md-1581-DONE-required execution and reuse use one bounded contract:
docs/requirements/decisions/proof-admissibility-hardening-execution-plan.md-1582-
docs/requirements/decisions/proof-admissibility-hardening-execution-plan.md-1583-- The DONE-required phase budget is the safe sum of effective sequential command timeouts plus bounded grace. A phase-specific override wins the global phase override, which wins the derived budget. The direct `done_required_validate` CLI max covers that derived phase; the `done_prepare` CLI max covers routine validation plus every enabled closeout phase. An explicit `LATTICE_MAX_TIMEOUT_MS` remains authoritative. Each effective command timeout is capped at Node's maximum legal timer delay before arming the real timer, so a huge configured value cannot overflow into an immediate timeout. Structured `failed` / `timed_out` / `blocked` results remain parseable on stdout and exit nonzero; routine `done_prepare` idle/max aborts use the same terminal timeout shape and release child processes, timers, and locks for an immediate rerun.
docs/requirements/decisions/proof-admissibility-hardening-execution-plan.md-1584-- `done_prepare` defaults `reuseFreshDoneRequired=true`, independently of post-closeout `reuseFreshValidation`. Reuse requires the canonical DONE-required evaluator to pass and evidence HEAD to equal current HEAD, or be its ancestor with every path touched by every intervening commit classified as trusted story metadata (including modify-then-revert history). HEAD must remain unchanged across evaluation. Any code, config, non-metadata, non-ancestor, unreadable evidence/lineage, or concurrent HEAD movement refuses reuse.
docs/requirements/decisions/proof-admissibility-hardening-execution-plan.md-1585-- `validate:false` means `disposition=skipped_explicitly` and `result=not_run`; it neither executes nor reuses nor manufactures evidence, while reporting `existingEvidenceBasis=fresh|stale|missing`. Executed and reused paths report `disposition`, `result`, `refusalReasons`, and any `timeoutLayer` in human and JSON output.
docs/requirements/decisions/proof-admissibility-hardening-execution-plan.md:1586:- Progress and heartbeat output uses stderr/the logging side channel, never JSON stdout. Reporter failures are diagnostic-only. Heartbeats refresh idle liveness only; command, phase, idle, and absolute max deadlines, child-tree termination, lock release, and timer cleanup remain independent.
